      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c13700c2_a9839d69",
        "filename": "board/samus_pd/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 193,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-29T16:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we got an interrupt since last enabling interrupts, we want to repeat the detection. I originally wrote the code \"if (!got_charger_interrupt[port]) task_wait_event(-1)\". But I decided on the above code, for this corner case:\n\n- got_charger_interrupt[port] \u003d\u003d 0 (no recent interrupt, so we decide to call task_wait_event)\n\n- Immediately afterward, the interrupt fires\n\n- ISR sets task event + sets got_charger_interrupt\n\n- ISR completes, we continue with task_wait_event call, discarding the pending event (I think) and waiting for a new event which will never come (because pericom won\u0027t fire a new interrupt until we clear the old one manually)\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "a12ccc7b_a872bbd2",
      "revId": "982e49402cc1ebf95bebc48876b09e122e508eda",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
